From: robertijtsma <37256770+robertijtsma@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: videocc-sm8150: add qcom,sc8180x-videocc compatible

The SC8180X video clock controller at 0xab00000 exposes the same
register layout, PLL, branch clocks, resets, and GDSCs (venus_gdsc,
vcodec0_gdsc, vcodec1_gdsc) as SM8150, and upstream sc8180x.dtsi lists
compatible = "qcom,sc8180x-videocc", "qcom,sm8150-videocc".

Add an explicit qcom,sc8180x-videocc match entry so the module binds
cleanly when built out-of-tree or enabled via CONFIG_SM_VIDEOCC_8150.
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/videocc-sm8150.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/videocc-sm8150.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/videocc-sm8150.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/videocc-sm8150.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/videocc-sm8150.c
@@ -233,6 +233,7 @@ static const struct qcom_cc_desc video_cc_sm8150_desc = {
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id video_cc_sm8150_match_table[] = {
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sc8180x-videocc" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8150-videocc" },
 	{ }
 };
-- 
2.47.0
